              W7 test gate runs the headless TeslaSync.App.Tests project (the sibling-W7 convention).

=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free projection,
  unit-tested headlessly), optionally <Name>.Source.cs, <Name>.ViewModel.cs (the state holder) and <Name>.cs (the
  Fluent view) — exactly as the sibling W7 DevToolsPage / FeatureFlagsPage / TeslaChargingSessionsPage do. The
  generated prompt's idealized "TeslaOrdersPage.xaml + TeslaOrdersPageViewModel.cs under TeslaSync/Features/Admin"
  is mapped onto these real conventions; the surface registers with the W4 ShellPageFactory by route name
  ("TeslaOrders", already in RouteTable.cs → /tesla-orders, RouteGroup.AdminDevTools).
- The web page is a thin wrapper — `<PageContainer title={t('orders.title')} subtitle={t('orders.subtitle')}>
  <ActiveOrdersSection /></PageContainer>`. The native port reproduces that shell exactly: the page HOSTS the
  shared W3 ActiveOrdersSection surface (already implemented under feature-views/ActiveOrdersSection, namespace
  TeslaSync.App.FeatureViews.Settings — the web also imports the section from features/settings/components) inside
  the native shared-surfaces PageContainer (the parity port of web/src/components/layout/PageContainer.tsx,
  constructed `new PageContainer(localizer, title) { Subtitle, PageContent }`, the DevToolsPage host precedent).
  The ActiveOrdersSection owns every order card and ALL of its loading / empty / error / populated + stale/offline
  states; the page owns only the title + subtitle chrome — the two parity strings.
- Data binding (ADR-004): the page parity unit declares NO API data sources of its own (the manifest record:
  "renders from navigation params / local state"); the order data belongs to the hosted ActiveOrdersSection (its
  own W3 unit, bound to get_api_v1_tesla_user_orders / post_api_v1_tesla_user_orders_refresh). Following the
  established host-injection precedent (every feature page's parameterless ctor defaults to an Empty feed; an
  explicit ctor accepts the generated-client source for tests/DI), the page hosts the section over
  EmptyActiveOrdersSource by default — a single successful-but-empty snapshot so the section renders its honest
  pre-fetch empty body ("No order data yet. Click Refresh to fetch from Tesla."), with the explicit
  TeslaOrdersPage(IActiveOrdersSource, ILocalizer) ctor for the live source. No HTTP touches the page.
- The two parity strings resolve through the ILocalizer facade with the web key names + English defaults
  (TeslaOrdersRegistration.Title/Subtitle → translation.orders.title / translation.orders.subtitle). These are
  the SAME web i18n keys the hosted ActiveOrdersSection uses (the web repeats t('orders.title') / t('orders.subtitle')
  in both the page and the section), and they already exist verbatim in Strings/{en,he,ar}/Resources.resw — so NO
  string-catalog change was needed. The TeslaOrdersPageViewModel exposes Title/Subtitle and a Reload() that
  re-resolves them after a language change (react-i18next parity).
- a11y (ADR-015): the page is an AutomationControlType.Group with an AutomationProperties.Name of the resolved
  title; the hosted PageContainer renders the title at heading-level 1 and the section carries its own Narrator
  names. Dark/light theming + tokens come from the composed shared surfaces (no hardcoded colors). SI units N/A
  for this admin chrome (the order cards' fields are model/status/VIN/dates — no unit-bearing quantities).

